  "notes": [
    "SDBH carries NO LEXEntryCode on any of its 16224 meanings; SDGNT carries one on essentially all of its. The Louw-Nida key exists on the Greek side only, and MACULA already ships it on our Greek tokens.",
    "Domain codes are namespaced. 1112 keys, all prefixed \"sdbh:\" or \"louw-nida:\". 18 bare codes collide between the two trees with zero label agreement, so a bare code is never a valid key.",
    "SDBH StrongCodes rejected by reason: {\"empty\":26,\"prose-not-a-code\":3,\"bare-number\":2}. These are upstream data defects, not parser failures; each is recorded, none guessed.",
    "655 SDBH codes used the Aramaic \"A\" sigil and were rewritten A→H with the number untouched (Strong's interleaves Aramaic in the one H series; proved against bdb-kjv.json H3/H4, H69, H412).",
    "3 numbers carry both an H and an A code across different entries (H3879, H6211, H8412); each looks like an upstream off-by-one. NOT merged.",
    "38 Hebrew and 4 Greek canonical keys are claimed as an identity by more than one entry.",
    "281 SDBH and 6 SDGNT codes are constituent claims from a multi-word headword, routed to byStrongConstituent so \"Ebenezer\" never attaches to every occurrence of \"stone\".",
    "2697 SDBH and 264 SDGNT LEXReferences values carry an inline {N:nnn} footnote marker inside the reference string, making the field variable-length. All handled.",
    "LEXReferences word field is an EVEN-numbered MORPHEME ordinal (word/2), not a token ordinal. Our tokens keep Hebrew prefixes glued, so word-level joins need the package change in docs/step-word-card-parity.md §2 field 40. Verse-level joins work now."
  ],
